     1→# Feature: Improve Pokemon View
     2→
     3→## Feature Description
     4→Enhance the Pokemon detail view to display comprehensive information in a friendly, well-organized layout. The current implementation shows only basic information (name, types, and simple stats). This feature will add sprite images with shiny toggle functionality, a structured stats table with highlighting, detailed abilities with tooltips, and evolution chain navigation buttons. The enhancement will create a richer, more interactive experience that helps users explore Pokemon data more effectively.
     5→
     6→## User Story
     7→As a Pokemon database user
     8→I want to view comprehensive Pokemon information in a well-organized layout with interactive elements
     9→So that I can easily understand Pokemon characteristics, abilities, and evolution relationships
    10→
    11→## Problem Statement
    12→The current Pokemon detail view is minimal and doesn't leverage the rich data available from the PokeAPI. Users cannot:
    13→- See what Pokemon look like (no sprite images)
    14→- Easily compare stats or identify strongest attributes
    15→- Understand ability effects without navigating away
    16→- Navigate through evolution chains
    17→- View shiny variants
    18→- See the Pokedex number prominently displayed
    19→
    20→This limited presentation makes it difficult for users to get a complete picture of a Pokemon's characteristics and relationships.
    21→
    22→## Solution Statement
    23→Transform the Pokemon detail view into a comprehensive information display by:
    24→- Adding the Pokedex number next to the Pokemon name (right-aligned)
    25→- Displaying Pokemon sprite images (default and shiny variants) with click-to-toggle functionality
    26→- Restructuring stats into a 2x3 table layout with the highest stat highlighted
    27→- Showing abilities with their flavor text and hover tooltips for full descriptions
    28→- Adding evolution navigation buttons (pre-evolution and evolution) with appropriate arrows
    29→- Removing redundant "Types" section title for cleaner presentation
    30→- Fetching additional data from PokeAPI (sprites, stats, abilities, species/evolution chain)
    31→- Creating comprehensive E2E tests for all new interactive features
    32→
    33→## Relevant Files
    34→Use these files to implement the feature:
    35→
    36→- **app/server/src/services/pokeapi.js** - Service layer for PokeAPI integration. Currently fetches basic Pokemon data (name, types, id, height, weight). Needs to be extended to fetch sprites, stats, abilities, and species/evolution chain data.
    37→
    38→- **app/server/src/routes/pokemon.js** - API route handler for Pokemon endpoints. Passes through data from pokeapi service. May need updates if response structure changes significantly.
    39→
    40→- **app/client/src/utils/api.js** - Client-side API utility for fetching Pokemon data. Should continue to work with enhanced data structure from backend.
    41→
    42→- **app/client/src/components/PokemonDetail/PokemonDetail.jsx** - Main Pokemon detail component. Needs significant updates to display: Pokedex number, sprite images with toggle, stats table, abilities with tooltips, and evolution navigation.
    43→
    44→- **app/client/src/components/PokemonDetail/PokemonDetail.css** - Styles for Pokemon detail component. Needs new styles for: image display, stats table layout, ability cards with tooltips, evolution navigation buttons, and highlight colors.
    45→
    46→- **app/client/src/App.jsx** - Main app component managing state and navigation. May need minor updates if evolution navigation requires Pokemon selection changes.
    47→
    48→### New Files
    49→- **e2e/pokemon-detail-enhancements.spec.js** - E2E test suite for new Pokemon detail functionality including image toggle, ability tooltips, stat highlighting, evolution navigation, and API data validation.
    50→
    51→## Implementation Plan
    52→
    53→### Phase 1: Foundation
    54→Extend the backend API service to fetch comprehensive Pokemon data from PokeAPI. This includes sprites (default and shiny), base stats, abilities with descriptions, and species data for evolution chain information. Update the data transformation layer to structure this information for frontend consumption while maintaining backwards compatibility.
    55→
    56→### Phase 2: Core Implementation
    57→Transform the Pokemon detail component to display the enhanced data in an organized layout. Implement the 2x3 stats table with highlighting logic, sprite image display with toggle functionality, ability cards with hover tooltips, and visual layout improvements. Add state management for image toggle between default and shiny sprites.
    58→
    59→### Phase 3: Integration
    60→Add evolution chain navigation by fetching species data and implementing navigation buttons that trigger Pokemon selection changes. Integrate with existing App.jsx state management to ensure smooth navigation. Create comprehensive E2E tests to validate all interactive features and data accuracy.
    61→
    62→## Step by Step Tasks
    63→IMPORTANT: Execute every step in order, top to bottom.
    64→
    65→### 1. Extend Backend API - Fetch Additional Pokemon Data
    66→- Open `app/server/src/services/pokeapi.js`
    67→- Update the `getPokemonByName` function to fetch additional data from the Pokemon API response:
    68→  - Sprites: `response.data.sprites.front_default` and `response.data.sprites.front_shiny`
    69→  - Stats: `response.data.stats` array (hp, attack, defense, special-attack, special-defense, speed)
    70→  - Abilities: `response.data.abilities` array with ability names and URLs
    71→- Add a new function `getAbilityDetails(abilityUrl)` to fetch ability descriptions from the PokeAPI:
    72→  - Fetch from ability URL
    73→  - Extract `flavor_text_entries` (short description) in English
    74→  - Extract `effect_entries` (full effect description) in English
    75→  - Return both flavor text and effect text
    76→- Add a new function `getSpeciesData(pokemonId)` to fetch evolution chain information:
    77→  - Fetch from `https://pokeapi.co/api/v2/pokemon-species/{id}`
    78→  - Extract `evolution_chain.url`
    79→  - Fetch evolution chain from that URL
    80→  - Parse the chain to identify pre-evolution and evolution Pokemon names
    81→  - Return an object with `preEvolution` and `evolution` properties
    82→- Update the `getPokemonByName` return object to include:
    83→  - `sprites: { default: string, shiny: string }`
    84→  - `stats: [{ name: string, value: number }]`
    85→  - `abilities: [{ name: string, flavorText: string, effect: string }]`
    86→  - `evolution: { preEvolution: string|null, evolution: string|null }`
    87→- Add proper error handling for cases where sprites, abilities, or evolution data are not available
    88→- Ensure all API calls have appropriate timeouts
    89→
    90→### 2. Update Pokemon Detail Component - Add State for Image Toggle
    91→- Open `app/client/src/components/PokemonDetail/PokemonDetail.jsx`
    92→- Import `useState` from React at the top of the file
    93→- Add state variable: `const [showShiny, setShowShiny] = useState(false);`
    94→- Add effect to reset shiny state when Pokemon changes: `useEffect(() => { setShowShiny(false); }, [pokemon?.name]);`
    95→- Create toggle handler: `const handleImageClick = () => { setShowShiny(!showShiny); };`
    96→
    97→### 3. Update Pokemon Detail Component - Redesign Layout Structure
    98→- In `app/client/src/components/PokemonDetail/PokemonDetail.jsx`, restructure the JSX:
    99→  - Move Pokedex number next to the Pokemon name (in header section)
   100→  - Add image section below the name (before types)
   101→  - Remove the "Types" h2 section title, keep just the badges
   102→  - Add stats section with 2x3 table layout below types
   103→  - Add abilities section below stats
   104→  - Add evolution navigation section at the bottom
   105→- Implement the header with name and Pokedex number:
   106→  ```jsx
   107→  <div className="pokemon-header">
   108→    <h1 className="pokemon-name">{pokemon.name}</h1>
   109→    {pokemon.id && <span className="pokedex-number">#{pokemon.id}</span>}
   110→  </div>
   111→  ```
   112→
   113→### 4. Update Pokemon Detail Component - Add Sprite Image Display
   114→- Add image section after the header:
   115→  ```jsx
   116→  <div className="pokemon-image-section">
   117→    {pokemon.sprites?.default ? (
   118→      <img
   119→        src={showShiny && pokemon.sprites.shiny ? pokemon.sprites.shiny : pokemon.sprites.default}
   120→        alt={`${pokemon.name} sprite`}
   121→        className="pokemon-sprite"
   122→        onClick={handleImageClick}
   123→        title={showShiny ? "Click to show default sprite" : "Click to show shiny sprite"}
   124→      />
   125→    ) : (
   126→      <div className="no-image-message">No image available</div>
   127→    )}
   128→    {pokemon.sprites?.shiny && (
   129→      <div className="sprite-label">{showShiny ? "Shiny" : "Default"}</div>
   130→    )}
   131→  </div>
   132→  ```
   133→
   134→### 5. Update Pokemon Detail Component - Add Stats Table with Highlighting
   135→- Calculate the maximum stat value to determine which stat to highlight
   136→- Add stats section with 2x3 table layout:
   137→  ```jsx
   138→  {pokemon.stats && pokemon.stats.length > 0 && (
   139→    <div className="pokemon-info-section">
   140→      <h2 className="section-title">Stats</h2>
   141→      <div className="stats-table">
   142→        <div className="stat-row">
   143→          <div className={`stat-cell ${isMaxStat('hp')}`}>
   144→            <span className="stat-name">HP</span>
   145→            <span className="stat-value">{getStatValue('hp')}</span>
   146→          </div>
   147→          <div className={`stat-cell ${isMaxStat('speed')}`}>
   148→            <span className="stat-name">Speed</span>
   149→            <span className="stat-value">{getStatValue('speed')}</span>
   150→          </div>
   151→        </div>
   152→        {/* Repeat for attack/defense, special-attack/special-defense */}
   153→      </div>
   154→    </div>
   155→  )}
   156→  ```
   157→- Add helper functions to get stat values and determine max stat
   158→- Ensure stat values are displayed in bold
   159→
   160→### 6. Update Pokemon Detail Component - Add Abilities with Tooltips
   161→- Add abilities section below stats:
   162→  ```jsx
   163→  {pokemon.abilities && pokemon.abilities.length > 0 && (
   164→    <div className="pokemon-info-section">
   165→      <h2 className="section-title">Abilities</h2>
   166→      <div className="abilities-list">
   167→        {pokemon.abilities.map((ability, index) => (
   168→          <div key={index} className="ability-card" title={ability.effect}>
   169→            <div className="ability-name">{ability.name}</div>
   170→            <div className="ability-flavor">{ability.flavorText}</div>
   171→          </div>
   172→        ))}
   173→      </div>
   174→    </div>
   175→  )}
   176→  ```
   177→- Use the native `title` attribute for tooltip functionality
   178→
   179→### 7. Update Pokemon Detail Component - Add Evolution Navigation
   180→- Add evolution navigation section at the bottom:
   181→  ```jsx
   182→  {pokemon.evolution && (
   183→    <div className="pokemon-info-section">
   184→      <h2 className="section-title">Evolution</h2>
   185→      <div className="evolution-navigation">
   186→        <button
   187→          className="evolution-btn pre-evolution"
   188→          disabled={!pokemon.evolution.preEvolution}
   189→          onClick={() => pokemon.evolution.preEvolution && onSelectPokemon(pokemon.evolution.preEvolution)}
   190→        >
   191→          {pokemon.evolution.preEvolution && (
   192→            <>
   193→              <span className="evolution-arrow">←</span>
   194→              <span className="evolution-name">{pokemon.evolution.preEvolution}</span>
   195→            </>
   196→          )}
   197→        </button>
