   452→- Add test to verify disabled state for Pokemon without pre-evolution (e.g., starter Pokemon)
   453→- Add test to verify disabled state for Pokemon without evolution (e.g., final evolution)
   454→- Verify buttons show correct Pokemon names and arrow directions
   455→
   456→### 20. Create E2E Tests - API Data Validation
   457→- Add test to verify correct data is fetched from backend API
   458→- Validate that Pokemon details include all new fields (sprites, stats, abilities, evolution)
   459→- Add test for error handling when Pokemon data is incomplete
   460→- Test API response structure matches expected format
   461→
   462→### 21. Create E2E Tests - Types Section Update
   463→- Add test to verify "Types" section title is removed
   464→- Verify type badges are still displayed correctly
   465→- Ensure types appear in correct position (below image, above stats)
   466→
   467→### 22. Run Validation Commands
   468→- Execute `npm run test:e2e` to run all E2E tests
   469→- Verify all new tests pass with zero failures
   470→- Check that existing Pokemon search and API tests still pass (no regressions)
   471→- Manually test the application by starting both client and server
   472→- Verify all interactive features work correctly in the browser
   473→
   474→## Testing Strategy
   475→
   476→### Unit Tests
   477→No unit tests are required for this feature as it primarily involves UI enhancements and data transformation. The backend service functions should be tested through E2E tests that validate the complete data flow.
   478→
   479→### Integration Tests
   480→E2E tests will serve as integration tests, validating:
   481→- Backend API correctly fetches and structures data from PokeAPI
   482→- Frontend correctly displays all data fields
   483→- Interactive features (image toggle, navigation) work correctly
   484→- Data flows properly from API through backend to frontend
   485→
   486→### Edge Cases
   487→- Pokemon without sprite images (show "No image available" message)
   488→- Pokemon without shiny sprites (disable toggle functionality or show same image)
   489→- Pokemon at the start of evolution chain (pre-evolution button disabled)
   490→- Pokemon at the end of evolution chain (evolution button disabled)
   491→- Pokemon with no evolution chain (both buttons disabled)
   492→- Pokemon with single ability vs multiple abilities
   493→- Pokemon with missing ability descriptions
   494→- Pokemon with very long ability descriptions (tooltip should handle overflow)
   495→- API timeouts or failures (display appropriate error messages)
   496→- Pokemon with tied stats (multiple stats with same highest value - highlight all)
   497→
   498→## Acceptance Criteria
   499→- [ ] Pokedex number is displayed on the right side next to Pokemon name with "#" prefix
   500→- [ ] Pokemon sprite image is displayed below the name and above types
   501→- [ ] Clicking the sprite image toggles between default and shiny versions
   502→- [ ] "No image available" message appears when sprite is not available
   503→- [ ] Sprite label indicates "Default" or "Shiny" based on current display
   504→- [ ] "Types" section title is removed, but type badges remain visible
   505→- [ ] Stats are displayed in a 2x3 table format (HP/Speed, Attack/Defense, SpAtk/SpDef)
   506→- [ ] Each stat shows name and value, with value in bold
   507→- [ ] The highest stat value is highlighted with green color (not red)
   508→- [ ] Abilities are listed below stats with name and flavor text
   509→- [ ] Hovering over an ability displays a tooltip with the full effect description
   510→- [ ] Evolution navigation buttons are displayed at the bottom
   511→- [ ] Pre-evolution button shows left arrow and Pokemon name (or is disabled if none)
   512→- [ ] Evolution button shows Pokemon name and right arrow (or is disabled if none)
   513→- [ ] Clicking evolution buttons navigates to the respective Pokemon
   514→- [ ] Backend API successfully fetches sprites, stats, abilities, and evolution data
   515→- [ ] All E2E tests pass, including new tests for image toggle, tooltips, and navigation
   516→- [ ] No regressions in existing search and API functionality
   517→- [ ] Application handles all edge cases gracefully (missing data, API failures, etc.)
   518→
   519→## Validation Commands
   520→Execute every command to validate the feature works correctly with zero regressions.
   521→
   522→- `npm run dev:client` - Start client development server (manual testing)
   523→- `npm run dev:server` - Start server development server (manual testing)
   524→- `npm run test:e2e` - Run all E2E tests including new Pokemon detail enhancement tests
   525→- `npm run test:e2e:headed` - Run E2E tests in headed mode to visually verify interactions
   526→
   527→## Notes
   528→
   529→### PokeAPI Data Structure
   530→- Pokemon endpoint: `https://pokeapi.co/api/v2/pokemon/{name}`
   531→  - Sprites: `sprites.front_default` and `sprites.front_shiny`
   532→  - Stats: `stats` array with `stat.name` and `base_stat`
   533→  - Abilities: `abilities` array with `ability.name` and `ability.url`
   534→- Ability endpoint: `https://pokeapi.co/api/v2/ability/{id}`
   535→  - Flavor text: `flavor_text_entries` (filter for English language)
   536→  - Effect: `effect_entries` (filter for English language)
   537→- Species endpoint: `https://pokeapi.co/api/v2/pokemon-species/{id}`
   538→  - Evolution chain URL: `evolution_chain.url`
